Contributing to Lughnasadh
==========================

Lughnasadh follows a progressive free-software lab practice:

1. Prefer clarity over micro-optimization unless measured.
2. Keep UCI compatible (Sherlock and other GUIs depend on it).
3. Document user-visible changes in NEWS; technical notes in ChangeLog / doc/.
4. Prep/analysis only — do not add features whose primary purpose is
   live cheating in official events.
5. Open a pull request against main with a short rationale and build proof.

Coding
------
* C++20
* cmake -B build && cmake --build build -j
* Run the UCI smoke from INSTALL before sending a PR
